# Design: Four-second open reply wait

## Problem
The viewer binds open.sock before its event loop drains requests.
On a loaded macos runner the first reply took over the 2 s wait, so
the healthy viewer answered OPERATION_UNAVAILABLE (desk_open flake,
nightly run 41027528544).

## Approach
Raise the server-side wait to 4 s. The client caps at 5 s
(DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS is 10 s, open_at clamps to 5 s), so a truly
unanswered request still surfaces the same bounded messages.

## Rejected alternative
Retrying in open_at. A re-send queues a second request behind the
first undrained one; the full sync channel then answers
"viewer busy", and transport_bounds_invalid_busy_unresponsive_and_
expired_requests pins that a queued, never-drained request must
surface "unresponsive". The retry failed that test locally.
